From: Gran Turismo 6 for Mac <https://github.com/Wooloomooloo2/Gran-Turismo-6-Mac>
Subject: [PATCH] cellOskDialog: the on-screen keyboard's events, result and text

Upstream: not yet submitted; written to be upstreamed (generic)
Licence: MIT, as ps3recomp (see its LICENSE); offered under the same terms
Base: ps3recomp 4e8f3ca87a3e1d87bb83b8b7e9348fe2685cd514 (after 0001-0048)

What: the module was a stub that needed a cellOskDialogInit no SDK has, so
LoadAsync answered NOT_INITIALIZED, posted no event, and four of GT6's
imports (DisableDimmer, SetKeyLayoutOption, ExtSetInitialScale,
ExtRegisterForceFinishCallback) were unresolved: its player-name page never
got a keyboard. Now LoadAsync checks its arguments (PARAM for a missing
param, message or initial text, or a limit over 512; BUSY while open) and
posts CELL_SYSUTIL_OSKDIALOG_LOADED to every registered sysutil callback.
The host answers on a later cellSysutilCheckCallback (PS3_OSK_DELAY_MS,
default 1000 ms): it confirms with the next entry of PS3_OSK_TEXT
(comma-separated, one per dialog) or else the initial text, or cancels with
PS3_OSK_CANCEL=1, and posts FINISHED. UnloadAsync returns the result and
the text NUL-terminated (corrected by 0051: cut to numCharsResultString characters, the NUL after them) and posts UNLOADED;
GetInputText reports NO_INPUT_TEXT until then; Abort gives ABORT and posts
FINISHED. GetSize writes u16s and takes the dialog type. The SDK's error
codes (0x8002B501-4) replace invented ones.
Reference: the SDK's cellOskDialog documentation, with RPCS3's
cellOskDialog.cpp as the behaviour reference only; no emulator code.
cellSysutilCheckCallback calls cellOskDialog_tick (the host's answer), so
the sysutil test fixtures that stub cellMsgDialog_tick stub it too.
Tests: libs/misc/tests/test_osk_dialog.c (tools/test_osk_dialog.py), which
also checks the four names hash to GT6's imported NIDs.
diff --git a/libs/misc/cellOskDialog.c b/libs/misc/cellOskDialog.c
index 17e7c674..ac4d731f 100644
--- a/libs/misc/cellOskDialog.c
+++ b/libs/misc/cellOskDialog.c
@@ -1,277 +1,355 @@
 /*
  * ps3recomp - cellOskDialog HLE implementation
  *
- * Provides an on-screen keyboard stub.  When a game requests text input,
- * the prompt is logged and an empty string (or configurable default) is
- * returned immediately.  In a full implementation this would show an
- * actual input dialog.
+ * The system's on-screen keyboard, as the title sees it. LoadAsync opens the
+ * dialog and the system posts CELL_SYSUTIL_OSKDIALOG_LOADED to every
+ * registered sysutil callback; when the user confirms (or cancels) it posts
+ * FINISHED; the title then calls UnloadAsync, which hands back the result and
+ * the text and posts UNLOADED. GetInputText reads the text while it is open.
+ * Abort closes it with the ABORT result and posts FINISHED.
+ *
+ * There is no keyboard on screen here. The "user" is the host: the dialog is
+ * confirmed a short time after it opens (PS3_OSK_DELAY_MS, default 1000, so
+ * the title sees LOADED and FINISHED on different polls, as it would with a
+ * person typing) with the next entry of PS3_OSK_TEXT (comma-separated ASCII,
+ * one entry per dialog, for scripted runs), or, past the list or without it,
+ * the dialog's initial text unchanged -- what pressing Start on the PS3's
+ * keyboard does. PS3_OSK_CANCEL=1 cancels instead. A Mac text field is the
+ * player's version of this (BACKLOG, Mac GUI).
+ *
+ * Errors and argument checks follow the SDK's documented codes, with RPCS3's
+ * cellOskDialog.cpp as the behaviour reference (no code taken from it).
+ * Guest structs (all pointers are 4-byte guest addresses, big-endian):
+ *   CellOskDialogInputFieldInfo      { u16* message; u16* init_text; u32 limit_length; }
+ *   CellOskDialogCallbackReturnParam { s32 result; s32 numCharsResultString; u16* pResultString; }
+ *   CellOskDialogParam               { u32 allowOskPanelFlg; u32 firstViewPanel;
+ *                                      f32 controlPoint.x, .y; s32 prohibitFlgs; }
  */
 
 #include "cellOskDialog.h"
+#include "../system/cellSysutil.h"   /* cellSysutilQueueEvent, CELL_SYSUTIL_MAX_CALLBACKS */
 #include <stdio.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
 #include <string.h>
-#include "../../runtime/ppu/ppu_memory.h"   /* vm_write*: guest EA -> host, byte-swapped */
-#include "../guest_struct.h"   /* GUEST_EA, vm_read/vm_write: guest EA -> host */
+#include "../../runtime/ppu/ppu_memory.h"   /* vm_read/vm_write: guest EA -> host, byte-swapped */
+#include "../../runtime/ppu/ppu_context.h"
+#include "../guest_struct.h"                /* GUEST_EA */
+#ifdef _WIN32
+#  include <windows.h>
+#else
+#  include <pthread.h>
+#  include <time.h>
+#endif
